title: 'frame-benchmarking: fall back to median value for same-x samples in `min_squares_iqr`'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Fixes a regression where `benchmark pallet --output` has been failing with
      "Parameter `n` only has 1 unique value(s)" for benchmarks touching a distinct storage key
      per item. The per-prefix proof-size analysis can see one or two samples sharing a single
      component value, and `min_squares_iqr` now uses the median value for those instead of
      erroring. Two samples at distinct values still get a fitted slope.

crates:
  - name: frame-benchmarking
    bump: patch
